1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,403
In this video, we're going to assemble
the 3D printed Braille embosser.

2
00:00:09,576 --> 00:00:11,311
Once everything has been fully

3
00:00:11,311 --> 00:00:14,814
3D printed, organize all of the parts
so that you can identify them.

4
00:00:15,115 --> 00:00:18,418
The embossing cylinder has raised
braille dots on the surface.

5
00:00:19,652 --> 00:00:22,555
The counter cylinder
is the one with recessed dots.

6
00:00:22,555 --> 00:00:25,792
Next, you have two different rollers
for the cylinders

7
00:00:26,893 --> 00:00:29,896
One holder has a plus sign.

8
00:00:30,463 --> 00:00:33,133
The other has a minus sign.

9
00:00:33,133 --> 00:00:36,636
The holder with the plus
sign is used with the embossing cylinder.

10
00:00:37,170 --> 00:00:40,340
The holder with the minus
sign is used with the counter cylinder.

11
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:41,508
I recommend

12
00:00:41,508 --> 00:00:44,577
sorting these into two separate groups,
so you don't get the mixed up.

13
00:00:44,811 --> 00:00:49,449
Next, Slide, the plus sign holder,
into the embossing cylinder.

14
00:00:49,549 --> 00:00:51,317
To help guide you through this process,

15
00:00:51,317 --> 00:00:54,320
make sure that you line up
all of the triangle indicators.

16
00:00:54,421 --> 00:00:59,092
Every holder has a top triangle, Three
side triangles and a bottom triangle.

17
00:01:00,994 --> 00:01:02,395
I recommend testing the fit

18
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:05,398
by sliding the cylinder on only partway.

19
00:01:06,433 --> 00:01:09,669
The cylinder should go onto the holder,
without too much resistance.

20
00:01:09,869 --> 00:01:12,305
It shouldn't be too tight or too loose.

21
00:01:12,305 --> 00:01:14,607
If it feels too tight
and you might not be able to pull it

22
00:01:14,607 --> 00:01:17,610
back out, a little bit of sanding
might be needed.

23
00:01:18,545 --> 00:01:21,915
The fit seems right, so I’ll go ahead
and complete the assembly.

24
00:01:22,382 --> 00:01:25,785
All of the indicator triangles on the side
should be pointing to the right.

25
00:01:27,287 --> 00:01:30,290
Next, make sure that you're using
the minus sign holder.

26
00:01:31,591 --> 00:01:35,128
Make sure that the holder triangles
are facing the same direction

27
00:01:35,128 --> 00:01:38,131
as the cylinder triangles.

28
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:41,167
This time,

29
00:01:41,167 --> 00:01:44,170
the triangle should be facing to the left.

30
00:01:45,972 --> 00:01:48,708
When we bring these two cylinders
together, the indicator

31
00:01:48,708 --> 00:01:52,846
triangles on the top and the bottom
should be pointed directly at each other.

32
00:01:53,079 --> 00:01:55,815
And the indicator triangles on the sides
should mirror each other.

33
00:01:55,815 --> 00:01:58,384
The embossing cylinder’s triangles
pointing to the right

34
00:01:58,384 --> 00:02:00,620
and the counter
cylinder’s triangles pointing to the left.

35
00:02:01,888 --> 00:02:02,155
If you

36
00:02:02,155 --> 00:02:05,158
line it all up, the gears should interlock
seamlessly.

37
00:02:06,025 --> 00:02:08,895
Before moving on,
if you're using the optional grip

38
00:02:08,895 --> 00:02:11,898
extension,
it'll need to be installed next.

39
00:02:12,398 --> 00:02:15,401
The grip comes in two pieces;
a top piece and a bottom piece.

40
00:02:15,969 --> 00:02:18,538
I'll start by placing the top piece

41
00:02:18,538 --> 00:02:21,608
over the top of the base,
and then sliding it all the way down.

42
00:02:22,175 --> 00:02:25,845
Then set the bottom piece down
on a solid surface,

43
00:02:26,179 --> 00:02:29,082
and line up the top piece
and the base over it.

44
00:02:29,082 --> 00:02:32,085
It does take a little bit of effort,
but it should click in place.

45
00:02:33,753 --> 00:02:36,890
Once the extended grip is in place,
we can move on to the next steps.

46
00:02:37,657 --> 00:02:40,393
Before installing the rollers,
I recommend testing

47
00:02:40,393 --> 00:02:44,197
the fit of the lid, just to make sure that
it goes on and off cleanly.

48
00:02:45,532 --> 00:02:48,334
If it's too difficult to remove by hand,
I recommend,

49
00:02:48,334 --> 00:02:52,071
placing the lip of the lid
against a solid surface and pulling down.

50
00:02:52,172 --> 00:02:55,175
This should give you leverage
to pop it off without too much effort.

51
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:58,511
If the lid passes the check, we'll
go ahead and move on to the next step.

52
00:02:59,445 --> 00:03:02,282
This is the technique that works
best for me.

53
00:03:02,282 --> 00:03:05,818
I place both cylinders in my hand,
with my palm pointing up.

54
00:03:07,086 --> 00:03:10,356
I make sure that they're aligned correctly
and then hold the bottom in place

55
00:03:10,356 --> 00:03:11,891
with my fingers.

56
00:03:11,891 --> 00:03:15,528
Then, I grab the embosser base
with my other hand And double check

57
00:03:15,528 --> 00:03:18,531
that the plus sign is going in
to the left side,

58
00:03:18,531 --> 00:03:21,201
and the minus sign
is going into the right side.

59
00:03:21,201 --> 00:03:23,636
The embossing cylinder
should be on the left.

60
00:03:23,636 --> 00:03:25,505
And the counter
cylinder should be on the right.

61
00:03:26,773 --> 00:03:29,008
I then slide the cylinders and carefully.

62
00:03:29,008 --> 00:03:32,445
At about the halfway point, the rollers
should stay in place on their own.

63
00:03:33,112 --> 00:03:36,549
Once the rollers are in place,
do another check to make sure

64
00:03:36,549 --> 00:03:40,820
that the embossing cylinder is on the left
and has the X shape on top.

65
00:03:41,187 --> 00:03:44,224
The indicator triangles on top
and bottom should be pointing

66
00:03:44,224 --> 00:03:47,227
directly at each other,
and the side triangle should be mirrored.

67
00:03:47,427 --> 00:03:50,430
Next step is to install
the handle connector.

68
00:03:50,430 --> 00:03:53,132
The handle connector
has a matching X shape

69
00:03:53,132 --> 00:03:56,135
That should fit into the embossing
cylinder holder.

70
00:03:56,803 --> 00:03:59,806
Next, snap the lid back on.

71
00:04:02,375 --> 00:04:05,378
The last step is to attach the handle
grip.

72
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:09,949
Place the handle grip
on top of the handle connector

73
00:04:09,949 --> 00:04:12,952
and press down until it clicks into place.

74
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:17,357
Now go ahead and test it out
by giving the handle a couple of turns.

75
00:04:17,824 --> 00:04:21,027
It should feel a little stiff,
but not too difficult to rotate.

76
00:04:21,294 --> 00:04:23,796
if you're experiencing
a lot of resistance,

77
00:04:23,796 --> 00:04:25,832
double check
everything is aligned correctly.

78
00:04:26,799 --> 00:04:27,667
And that's it.

79
00:04:27,667 --> 00:04:30,470
Your 3D printed Braille
embosser is now fully assembled.
